{title: Blessed Be Your Glorious Name}
{subtitle: Ezra 2:40; Nehemiah 7:43; Ezra 3:9–10; Nehemiah 9:4–5; 9:5–7; 10:9–10}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Sev-en-ty-four of the [C#]sons of Hodaviah
[G#m]Returned from Babylon under the [D#m]sky
With Zerubbabel and [C#]Joshua we came
To [B]rebuild the [C#]house of the [D#m]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Kadmiel with his [C#]sons stood together
To [G#m]oversee those working on the holy [D#m]place
The foundation laid with [C#]care and reverence
[B]Priests in [C#]vestments with trumpets [D#m]raised
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Stand up and bless the [C#]LORD your God
From [G#m]everlasting to [D#m]everlasting
Blessed be your glorious [C#]name
Which is [G#m]exalted [A#]above ev[D#m]ery praise
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
On the platform of the Le[C#]vites
[G#m]Kadmiel cried out with a [D#m]loud voice
We recalled the sins of our [C#]fathers
And the [B]history [C#]of our [D#m]days
You [B]chose Abram [C#]from Ur of the [D#m]Chaldeans
And [B]gave [C#]him a new [A#]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Stand up and bless the [C#]LORD your God
From [G#m]everlasting to [D#m]everlasting
Blessed be your glorious [C#]name
Which is [G#m]exalted [A#m]above ev[D#m]ery praise
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
We placed our seal upon the co[C#]venant
To [G#m]follow the law and com[D#m]mandments
The wall is finished and the [C#]praise is sung
Our de[B]scendants [C#]join in the [D#m]song
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Stand up and bless the [C#]LORD your God
From [G#m]everlasting to [D#m]everlasting
Blessed be your glorious [C#]name
Which is [G#m]exalted [A#m]above ev[D#m]ery praise
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Blessed be your glorious [C#]name
A[G#m]bove every bles[A#m]sing and [D#m]praise
{end_of_verse}
